# Commit after each change

When a change in this repo is finished and correct, commit it in the same turn. Do not wait for the user to ask.

- One commit per logical change. Follow the repo's git commit rules (no config changes, no `--no-verify`, no force-push, no amend unless the user asked).
- Stage only the files that belong to that change. Leave secrets untracked.
- Commit message: one or two sentences on why.
- Push only when the user asks.
